{#-
  One schema becomes one Python package, and this is its `__init__.py`: the
  public surface of the package, and the aggregate that wires one repository
  per table onto one connection.

  Rendered once per schema, with the whole database in context and no object
  flag, per FR-RND-006:

      tpl -d <schema> render python/package > datalayer/<schema>/__init__.py

  It re-exports rather than declares. Everything a caller reaches is defined in
  a module beside this one — the errors and the connection in `_core`, a row
  and its filter in the table's own module — and this file names them in
  `__all__`, which is what makes them public under `mypy`'s
  `no_implicit_reexport`. A package whose `__init__` declared the errors would
  put every table module in an import cycle with it; `python/core.jinja` says
  why at more length.

  Together with `_core.py` this is where provenance is recorded. `now` is
  referenced nowhere in this example, per FR-CTX-030.
-#}
